{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted a research handoff product carrying one map refresh and one refined open premise, with preflight returning valid:true. Map refresh (map-v13.json, base version 12): an additive mapped surface records the verification quorum question that the previous Candidate opened and a served check answered - Raft.VerifyLeader quorum accounting - pointing at the client contract that returns the future and the heartbeat behaviour that delivers the counted acknowledgements, with the repair location still open; and the overview's open detail saying the verification reads were not traced to completion is replaced, because that path is no longer unread for the quorum question, while the remaining questions there (repair location, external consumers) are kept. Feedback: first, the verification path question is answered for the shipped path; second, the non-voter election premise is narrowed further - after the first prefix showed the non-voter campaigning and falling back while the voters elected among themselves, a second prefix lengthened every server's election timeout through the library's own configuration reload before the transfer so the voters should not have been campaigning, and the sampled sequence was again Candidate then Follower with no leadership, so the contending-voter-election explanation does not by itself account for the fallback. Remaining kept visible: the fallback mechanism is still unidentified since nothing in the grant path tests a candidate's suffrage, the transfer path still accepts a non-voter target and reports success with no leader established (no obligation covers it), both non-voter prefixes were draft exploration runs so no property evidence is claimed, the repair locations for the three newest obligations remain open, and the deferred third-party-transport, MonotonicLogStore and nested-module surfaces are unread. Run state: ten confirmed in-scope findings, all units checked, 2 audit units, 21 experiments, 11 semantic reviews and roughly nine minutes remaining.\"}"}}
